{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Data Warehouse"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about a data warehouse."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Design the data structure based on the database structures and its characteristics.  Understands the concept of data warehouse, its components and characteristics."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on the data validation and data warehouses."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "data warehouse"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a database designed for analysis of data"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A data warehouse is a database designed for analysis, not for real-time business operations."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob07aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "main "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "most important"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Do you know what its main features are? I ought to get informed about it. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob07aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "manager "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person in charge of a business "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Remember, a data houseware helps managers make decisions"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob07aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hidden "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not visible "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The third one is data mining; it can discover knowledge by finding hidden patterns."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob07aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "collect "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to obtain many ideas about something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: All information I've collected is going to help me understand if this is the solution our boss is looking for."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob07aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Future With the Present Simple - Interrogative Form"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>The <strong>present simple</strong> tense does not always refer to the present time. You can also use it to talk about the future.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>The <strong>present simple</strong> tense can also have a future connotation as it can refer to events that are scheduled or timetabled in the <strong>future</strong>. In order to change its connotation of time, we have to add a time expression right next to the sentence we write in <strong>present simple</strong>. As you are referring to specific events in a specific moment in the <strong>future</strong>, the time expressions that you use have to be as precise as possible; thus, expressions like <i>tonight at 9 o&rsquo;clock</i>, <i>in half an hour</i>, or <i>tomorrow at 6 pm</i> are needed.</p> <p>To make questions about the future using the <strong>present simple</strong>, use the following structures:</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">(Wh-) + <strong>Do / Does</strong> + Subject + <strong>Verb in base form</strong> + <strong>Complement </strong>?</p> <p>Example:</p> <p><i>What time <strong>does</strong> the software supplier office <strong>open</strong> <strong>tomorrow</strong>?</i></p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">(Wh-) + <strong>Be</strong> + Subject + <strong>Complement</strong>?</p> <p>Example:</p> <p><strong><i>Is</i></strong><i> the data warehouse <strong>available after 5 pm</strong>? </i></p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Does the meeting start at 8:30? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Does the boss leave in the afternoon?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "What is a data warehouse?"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Most companies have a data warehouse that helps to analyze information for making managerial decisions in the short and long term. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "A data warehouse is designed for analysis of business measures by categories and attributes; it is also optimized for bulk loads and large, complex, unpredictable queries that access many rows per table. A data warehouse is loaded with consistent, valid data, so it requires no real-time validation. Opposed to regular databases, a data warehouse supports few concurrent users."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "List the reasons a company needs a data warehouse for analysis. Write sentences using had better, ought to, or might want to."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Talk about the main features of a data warehouse in relation to a company you know."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write some ideas about the future of a company. Use be going to and will in your sentences. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your ideas with a partner. "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk about the reasons to consider a data warehouse."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I present information about the features of a data warehouse. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write down ideas about the future of a company using a data warehouse."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk to a partner about my findings."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n5le03ob07re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<p><strong>Jaime:</strong> Good morning, Sean. Does the meeting start at 8:30? Are you leaving already?<br /><strong>Sean:</strong> Hi! Yes, it does. I'll leave in a few minutes. Is there anything you need?<br /><strong>Jaime:</strong> Hmm, will you help me with something, please? I talked to the boss, and he asked me to find information about data warehouses. Do you know what those are?<br /><strong>Sean:</strong> Sure, I&rsquo;ll explain it to you. <br /><strong>Jaime:</strong> Great! I&rsquo;d better take notes, then.</p>"}, {"time": "25000", "image": "enpe8n5le03ob07re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<p><strong>Sean:</strong> Look, a data warehouse is a database designed for analysis, not for real-time business operations. It works with bulk loads and large queries, and it helps to understand information throughout time in a given company. <br /><strong>Jaime:</strong> I see. Do you know what its main features are? I ought to get informed about it. <br /><strong>Sean:</strong> OK, then. A data warehouse has some features: it&rsquo;s subject-oriented, integrated, time variant and non-volatile. In other words, you can define data by subject; the information appears in a consistent format, and it is used based on specific chunks of time. The information in the data warehouse does not change once is entered. Remember, a data houseware helps managers make decisions.</p>"}, {"time": "73000", "image": "enpe8n5le03ob07re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<p><strong>Jaime:</strong> Perfect. What else do you think I need to know?<br /><strong>Sean:</strong> Well, you might want to know that there are different types of data warehouses. Do you need to hand in this information today?<br /><strong>Jaime:</strong> Oh, I'm afraid so. Does the boss leave in the afternoon?<br /><strong>Sean:</strong> Yes, he does. Anyway, there are three different types of data warehouses. The first one is about information processing; it basically processes information by statistical analysis, charts, or graphs. The second one is about analytical processing; it supports analytical processing of information by Online Analytical Processing operations. The third one is data mining; it can discover knowledge by finding hidden patterns. This one can even show findings in a visual way. <br /><strong>Jaime:</strong> Wow. All information I've collected is going to help me understand if this is the solution our boss is looking for.</p>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n5le03ob07re1img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe8n5le03ob07re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}, {"template_override": 2, "contents": [{"value": {"video_src": "enpe8n5le03ob07re5vid01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "id": 0, "text": ""}]}, "type": "video"}], "type": "video", "_data": [{"type": "template_override", "content": 2}], "id": 3, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can tell what a data warehouse is.  "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Where do you think CEOs keep information for managerial decisions?"}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about the data warehouse main features. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "  I can describe the different types of data warehouses."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": 